  "query_preview": "..\n(Tomorrow through Saturday)\nIssued at 1122 AM CDT Sat Aug 29 2026\n\nThe anomalously strong upper level high will continue to sit nearly \noverhead Sunday and into early next week. Upper level heights and \ntemperatures will mostly be above the 90th percentile for this time \nof year. This will keep conditions hot and stagnant, with afternoon \nhighs remaining 98-103 and overnight lows in the 70s. Mostly trimmed \ntemperatures to slightly below NBM values, which look too hot \noverall. With continuous modest southerly flow, dew points will \ngradually rise. These factors will support afternoon heat indices of \n105-110 for good chunks of eastern OK and west- central AR. A Heat \nAdvisory is in effect Sunday for northeast OK, with additional \nheadlines likely in the coming days.\n\nFor the middle to end of next week the upper level high will \nslightly shift, and become centered just east of the area, with \nmoisture levels slowly climbing as this occurs. Overall, the same \ngeneral pattern of heat and dry weather will persist. However, the \nincrease in moisture will be just enough for at least the chance of \nsome higher terrain diurnal showers or storms (10-15 percent \nchance). Even longer range guidance (beyond day 7) has unusually \nhigh confidence in the upper level ridge remaining near or overhead \nthrough at least the next 10 days and likely beyond. \n\nFire weather concerns will continue each afternoon of the next week \ndue to hot, dry, and breezy conditions. Ensemble guidance shows \nSunday and Monday as the breeziest days overall.",
